EB = ED [03]
F,D,A are collinear [04]
FA = FD [05]
C,D,G are collinear [06]
F,E,G are collinear [07]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. C,A,B are collinear [00] & CA = CB [01] ⇒  C is midpoint of AB [08]
002. F,D,A are collinear [04] & FA = FD [05] ⇒  F is midpoint of AD [09]
003. C is midpoint of AB [08] & F is midpoint of AD [09] ⇒  CF ∥ BD [10]
004. D,E,B are collinear [02] & CF ∥ BD [10] ⇒  DE ∥ CF [11]
005. DE ∥ CF [11] & C,D,G are collinear [06] & F,E,G are collinear [07] ⇒  GD:GC = GE:GF [12]
006. D,E,B are collinear [02] & EB = ED [03] ⇒  E is midpoint of BD [13]
007. E is midpoint of BD [13] & F is midpoint of AD [09] ⇒  EF ∥ BA [14]
008. C,A,B are collinear [00] & F,E,G are collinear [07] & EF ∥ AB [14] ⇒  CA ∥ GF [15]
009. CA ∥ GF [15] & C,D,G are collinear [06] & F,D,A are collinear [04] ⇒  FD:FA = GD:GC [16]
010. GD:GC = GE:GF [12] & FD:FA = GD:GC [16] & FA = FD [05] ⇒  GE = GF
